# Forge accounts (git.telpher.stream logins) whose pull requests are certified through the
# project's sign-off ledger instead of a per-commit Signed-off-by: a maintainer reads each
# change on main after it lands and records a signed attestation (see AUTHORSHIP.md).
# One login per line. Read by scripts/dco-check.sh at the pull request's base commit, so while
# .gitea/workflows/dco.yml runs unchanged a pull request cannot exempt itself by adding its own
# account (one that edits that workflow is read for exactly that). The check blocks a merge only
# where it is required on the default branch, as legal-index's `just protect --apply` makes it
# once the kit has landed. Agents commit under these accounts and never write a human's sign-off.
